extends /template/newsentry.pug

block newsvariables
  - var newskey = '2018-08-24-best-paper-award-at-expressive-2018';

//-
  block date
    | [date]

  block title
    | [title]

block newscontent
  p.card-text
  p
    | The paper "MNPR: A Framework for Real-Time Expressive Non-Photorealistic Rendering of 3D Computer Graphics" by Santiago Montesdeoca, Hock Soon Seah, Amir Semmo, Pierre Bénard, Romain Vergne, Joelle Thollot, and Davide Benvenuti has received the Best Paper Award at this year's Joint Symposium on Computational Aesthetics, Sketch-Based Interfaces and Modeling, and Non-Photorealistic Animation and Rendering (Expressive). MNPR is a framework for expressive non-photorealistic rendering of 3D computer graphics that enables stylization pipelines with a wide range of control, thereby covering the interaction spectrum with real-time feedback. The framework has been open-sourced through this publication and is available from 
    a.external(href="http://github.com/semontesdeoca/MNPR" target="_blank") GitHub
    | . Expressive 2018 was held in Victoria, BC, Canada from the 17th to 19th August and was officially co-located with SIGGRAPH 2018.
